      "message": "Given that you assert in `RegisterSerialProcessor` that processors can only be added at the beginning of time, it feels like a bit of a waste to constantly be making copies of the vector here because we know it won\u0027t change by the time this method is called. (Assuming that you don\u0027t pass `kBeginningOfGPUTime` as the completed serial, anyway.\n\nI get why we want the processor list to be part of the state during startup, so I\u0027m not sure what I\u0027d suggest here. It\u0027s ultimately a pretty minor thing. But we DO want to reduce the amount of vector manipulation we do during steady state, so it\u0027s probably worth giving at least a bit of thought to.\n\nEDIT: Okay, I see that the processors could be altered by `AssumeCommandsComplete`, which might happen in parallel. Leaving this comment here just in case you can think of a way to reduce vector manipulation, but it\u0027s non-blocking.",
